WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
A mushroom digests its
food outside its body,

2
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.340
then absorbs the products.

3
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.220
It looks nothing like you.

4
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.770
Yet you are both eukaryotes.

5
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.570
Now meet some microbes with no nucleus.

6
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.860
Under the microscope, they
look just like bacteria.

7
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:20.410
So why are these look-alike microbes
placed further from bacteria than you are

8
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.820
from a mushroom?

9
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.340
In this mission, you'll see
what all living things share:

10
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:30.220
the same four kinds of
biochemical, plus DNA and ATP.

11
00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.870
Then you'll meet life's largest
groups, the three domains,

12
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.850
and place a newly found microbe yourself.

13
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.200
Your mission: explain why microbes that
look like bacteria can sit so far from

14
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:42.610
them.
